# Where a tutorial note stands (see tutwin.c): modes 2 to 6 of the note about the first unit's square, which place it by the square's
# side of the screen and height (tutwin_place): mode 2 at the left (the square is left of five eighths of the width), mode 3 at the
# right (the side limit moves an eighth in), mode 4 at the right and, the point being under a lower limit, below... the arrows
# leave the popup's top or bottom edge accordingly. Mode 6 sets no place for the popup (the popup's own). Each note has the Continue
# and End Tour buttons and is closed with Return.
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
26 state tw_seen 0x9a64ac 0x14
26 state tw_draw 0x8c9fd0 4
26 state tw_size 0x8c9f24 8
44 open tut_terrain_m2
50 snap mode2
52 key Return
56 open tut_terrain_m3
62 snap mode3
64 key Return
68 open tut_terrain_m4
74 snap mode4
76 key Return
80 open tut_terrain_m5
86 snap mode5
88 key Return
92 open tut_terrain_m6
98 snap mode6
100 key Return
104 snap closed
106 close
